A||N||2||Brian||Rear control arm bolts - size?||||1||
Z||000000||Brian||06-21-2001||07:54 AM||||In searching for the cause of some "wobble" in the rear end I found some play in a rear control arm mount.<P>It looks like a cradle repair was done incorrectly. Welded on plates block off the access holes to the mounting bolts.<BR>It looks to me like the control arm was mounted to the plate, positioned on the cradle & then welded. Naturally the rubber bushing didn't take too kindly to the heat. This overheated bushing is the source of the play. I can wiggle the control arm & see maybe 1/8" play at the bushing.<BR>Thinking that I might be able to tighten the bolt a bit & squash the bushing some I used a hole saw to reform the access holes.<BR>Surprise, surprise, the bolt head & nut are welded to the patch plates, in fact there's little or no head or nut visible because of the welding built up on them, sheesh!<BR>I'm almost willing to bet the original bolt was broken, God only knows what's welded in there now!<P><BR>The end result is, this job needs to be re-done properly. <BR>I know how it should be done & where I can have it done properly this time but......<P>I need to know the size of the original bolt, anyone know off hand?<BR>We're talking about an 86 SE here.<P>Thanx,<BR>Brian<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Steven||06-21-2001||10:33 AM||||The rear control arm bolt are GM # 11514112. They are Metric (M12 x 1.75 x 89). Nuts are 11515744 (M12 x 1.75)<P>------------------<BR>85 Fiero GT<BR>3.2 liter w/4sp manual trans<BR>Silver.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Brian||06-22-2001||06:22 AM||||Thanx,<P>It's much appreciated!<P>Brian||||reg||1
